Thought: Now I'll check the typical chemical shifts for carbon atoms to better understand the 13C NMR data.
Action: retrieve_carbon_shifts
Action Input: {}

Thought: Let me also check the aromatic proton shifts to better understand the aromatic region in the 1H NMR.
Action: retrieve_aromatic_protons_shifts
Action Input: {}

Thought: The simulated spectra for 2-acetylbenzoic acid doesn't match well with our data. Let me try 4-methylsalicylic acid (4-methyl-2-hydroxybenzoic acid), which would have a methyl group on the aromatic ring and both a carboxylic acid and a hydroxyl group:
Action: simulate_spectra
Action Input: {"smiles": "Cc1ccc(C(=O)O)c(O)c1"}

Thought: The 4-methylsalicylic acid doesn't match well either. Let me try 2-acetoxy-4-methylbenzoic acid, which would have a methyl group on the aromatic ring, a carboxylic acid group, and an acetoxy group:
Action: simulate_spectra
Action Input: {"smiles": "Cc1ccc(C(=O)O)c(OC(=O)C)c1"}

Thought: The 2-acetoxy-4-methylbenzoic acid is getting closer, but still doesn't match perfectly. Let me try 2-acetoxy-5-methylbenzoic acid (which is similar to aspirin but with a methyl group at the 5-position):
Action: simulate_spectra
Action Input: {"smiles": "Cc1ccc(OC(=O)C)c(C(=O)O)c1"}

Thought: Let me try 4-acetoxy-3-methylbenzoic acid:
Action: simulate_spectra
Action Input: {"smiles": "Cc1cc(C(=O)O)ccc1OC(=O)C"}

Thought: Let me try 5-acetyl-2-methylbenzoic acid, which would have a methyl group and an acetyl group on the aromatic ring, plus a carboxylic acid:
Action: simulate_spectra
Action Input: {"smiles": "Cc1ccc(C(=O)C)cc1C(=O)O"}

Thought: Let me try 2-formyl-4-methylbenzoic acid, which would have a methyl group, an aldehyde group, and a carboxylic acid:
Action: simulate_spectra
Action Input: {"smiles": "Cc1ccc(C(=O)O)c(C=O)c1"}

Thought: The 2-formyl-4-methylbenzoic acid is getting closer! The 1H NMR shows a singlet at 10.09 ppm for the aldehyde proton, which is close to our observed 10.50 ppm. Let me try 3-formyl-4-methylbenzoic acid:
Action: simulate_spectra
Action Input: {"smiles": "Cc1c(C=O)ccc(C(=O)O)c1"}

